  "7cba988e-da06-4e51-af46-67dae296cfef": {
   "id": "7cba988e-da06-4e51-af46-67dae296cfef",
   "message": {
    "id": "7cba988e-da06-4e51-af46-67dae296cfef",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1764396779.498,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "1. Find the kick's fundamental: put Fruity Parametric EQ 2 (or a spectrum analyzer like Wave Candy) on it and look for the low peak, e.g., ~55 Hz ≈ A1.\n2. In the Channel settings of the kick sampler, adjust the **pitch knob** (in semitones/cents) until the peak lands on your root or fifth. E.g., song in F minor → aim for F1 ≈ 43.7 Hz or C2 ≈ 65.4 Hz.\n3. Re-check against the 808: they should sound like one instrument at the downbeat, not two notes beating against each other."
     ]
    },
